{"title":"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A clock chimes once at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes past each hour and chimes on the hour according to the hour. For example, at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56f3ba6222e1ce7182d3b032fa31b97c32307e12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\text{PM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> there is one chime and at noon and midnight there are twelve chimes. Starting at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d770fb42d8dd44e091a511ecc7eff805ffdd6b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11:15 \\text{AM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da6d2fd138f3a091012c56f54963985f899cc62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{February 26, 2003},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"135\" height=\"15\" /> on what date will the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92bd23848268583d05014ad003a6aa7e40481d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003^{\\text{rd}}$\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> chime occur?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/008a983a8ce21eba32039a1de33f511321803548.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\text{March 8} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\text{March 9} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\text{March 10} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\text{March 20} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\text{March 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"631\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, find how many chimes will have already happened before midnight (the beginning of the day) of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc0ab7c246e9d01baccdd38c5882b5d55e107ec6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{February 27, 2003}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> half-hours have passed, and the number of chimes according to the hour is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33d4b43536e8237c758552fb3edfcfff8cd18d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+\\cdots+12.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"159\" height=\"14\" /> The total number of chimes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20f293d84173554e689cfe8462096b964769879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13+78=91.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Every day, there will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> half-hours and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb32e4e31d3a26f3852e3b7310144d46813390a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(1+2+3+\\cdots+12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" /> chimes according to the arrow, resulting in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/27491f9bec8a062b1e77d62dd39df7875e4fce17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24+156=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" /> total chimes.\n</p><p>On <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/5057dafc5b520d553ccfaaa38437f82a941e5c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{February 26},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> the number of chimes that still need to occur is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2c2f656b40e24dd4dfce5ccde5417312ed8940a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003-91=1912.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea1382fb93badd9010179511157dfa3cb8d33c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1912 \\div 180=10 \\text{R}112.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"171\" height=\"13\" /> Rounding up, it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> days past <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/5057dafc5b520d553ccfaaa38437f82a941e5c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{February 26},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5b63299709c1a913a1ebe7fa50d83e323370b8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) \\ } \\text{March 9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"113\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B\" title=\"2003 AMC 1